\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the benchmark. An entry $e=(h,R)$ supplies its header and exactly the papers the curators cited, each readable as full text, abstract or title only depending on open access; the causal gene is withheld. One model writes every draft and only the generation strategy varies: three paradigms, a memory-only control with no papers, and three add-ons (dashed, under their parent), each tested against its parent. The same claim-level audit, scoring and guards (Section~\ref {sec:strategies}) apply to every draft. The reference is curator-written per-paper text (OMIM allelic-variant descriptions in ClinVar), split once into fixed fact lists for the primary endpoint, plus HPO disease annotations, allelic variants, causal gene and inheritance for the secondary measures. Counts are for the 100-entry main set.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Overview of the benchmark. An entry $e=(h,R)$ supplies its header and exactly the papers the curators cited, each readable as full text, abstract or title only depending on open access; the causal gene is withheld. One model writes every draft and only the generation strategy varies: three paradigms, a memory-only control with no papers, and three add-ons (dashed, under their parent), each tested against its parent. The same claim-level audit, scoring and guards (Section~\ref {sec:strategies}) apply to every draft. The reference is curator-written per-paper text (OMIM allelic-variant descriptions in ClinVar), split once into fixed fact lists for the primary endpoint, plus HPO disease annotations, allelic variants, causal gene and inheritance for the secondary measures. Counts are for the 100-entry main set}{figure.1}{}}
