\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Where the facts direct reading did not fully convey went (97 entries, 466 paragraphs, 437 judge calls, none failed; left out: 3 entries whose writer was stopped). Each missed fact was checked once against the text available for its paper; the check is a model judgement. Bottom: by whether the draft conveyed the fact not at all (absent) or less precisely (partial). Facts contradicted by the draft (7 full text, 25 abstract, 0 title; 32 in all) are not in the columns.}}{25}{table.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_missed}{{18}{25}{Where the facts direct reading did not fully convey went (97 entries, 466 paragraphs, 437 judge calls, none failed; left out: 3 entries whose writer was stopped). Each missed fact was checked once against the text available for its paper; the check is a model judgement. Bottom: by whether the draft conveyed the fact not at all (absent) or less precisely (partial). Facts contradicted by the draft (7 full text, 25 abstract, 0 title; 32 in all) are not in the columns}{table.18}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Where the facts direct reading conveyed came from (97 entries, 466 paragraphs; pooled over facts; left out: 3 entries whose writer was stopped). Each fact the draft conveyed in full or in part was checked against the text the writer had for the paragraph's paper(s); a fact not stated there, or stated only partly, was checked once more against the text of the entry's other supplied papers, since a later paper may describe an earlier one. No fact went unjudged. A fact stated in no supplied text may have been recalled from memory, inferred from what the text states (for example an inheritance mode from zygosity), or misjudged; these are model judgements. Shares are of the facts in the row; ``either'': conveyed in full or in part.}}{26}{table.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_conveyed}{{19}{26}{Where the facts direct reading conveyed came from (97 entries, 466 paragraphs; pooled over facts; left out: 3 entries whose writer was stopped). Each fact the draft conveyed in full or in part was checked against the text the writer had for the paragraph's paper(s); a fact not stated there, or stated only partly, was checked once more against the text of the entry's other supplied papers, since a later paper may describe an earlier one. No fact went unjudged. A fact stated in no supplied text may have been recalled from memory, inferred from what the text states (for example an inheritance mode from zygosity), or misjudged; these are model judgements. Shares are of the facts in the row; ``either'': conveyed in full or in part}{table.19}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces OMIM facts conveyed restricted by whether the supplied text states the fact (93 compared entries). Each fixed fact carries one judgement of whether the text available for its paper states it, partly states it or does not state it (a model judgement; a ``stated'' verdict needs a quote verified in the text; not checked by a curator); it is the same for every strategy. Top: the facts by how the paragraph's paper could be read (pooled; identical for every strategy). Middle: coverage as mean over entries / pooled over facts; $n$ = entries with facts in the restriction. Bottom: paired differences from direct reading in points (means over entries), bootstrap 95\% interval, entries better/worse/tied. The unrestricted means reproduce Table~\ref {tab:main}; the intervals here come from a separate bootstrap and can differ from it by 0.1.}}{26}{table.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_stated}{{20}{26}{OMIM facts conveyed restricted by whether the supplied text states the fact (93 compared entries). Each fixed fact carries one judgement of whether the text available for its paper states it, partly states it or does not state it (a model judgement; a ``stated'' verdict needs a quote verified in the text; not checked by a curator); it is the same for every strategy. Top: the facts by how the paragraph's paper could be read (pooled; identical for every strategy). Middle: coverage as mean over entries / pooled over facts; $n$ = entries with facts in the restriction. Bottom: paired differences from direct reading in points (means over entries), bootstrap 95\% interval, entries better/worse/tied. The unrestricted means reproduce Table~\ref {tab:main}; the intervals here come from a separate bootstrap and can differ from it by 0.1}{table.20}{}}
