\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces Hidden-full-text experiment, 46 entries and 136 paragraphs in every condition. Top: fixed fact lists (main measure), coverage pooled over facts and as a mean over entries, with the earlier per-draft scoring (pooled) beside it. The full-text draft is the main run's direct-reading draft; it went through the repair round and was also scored before repair; the two abstract drafts were not repaired. Before repair the audit flagged 13 of 6,609 audited claims (13 unsupported, 0 contradicted) in 11 paragraphs of 8 entries; repair revised those 11 paragraphs and deleted none. The draft before repair was reconstructed from the stored writer and audit replies without new generation (taking it through the repair round reproduces the final draft exactly). Middle: paired differences, means over entries. Bottom: earlier scoring, pooled over facts.}}{29}{table.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_hidden}{{24}{29}{Hidden-full-text experiment, 46 entries and 136 paragraphs in every condition. Top: fixed fact lists (main measure), coverage pooled over facts and as a mean over entries, with the earlier per-draft scoring (pooled) beside it. The full-text draft is the main run's direct-reading draft; it went through the repair round and was also scored before repair; the two abstract drafts were not repaired. Before repair the audit flagged 13 of 6,609 audited claims (13 unsupported, 0 contradicted) in 11 paragraphs of 8 entries; repair revised those 11 paragraphs and deleted none. The draft before repair was reconstructed from the stored writer and audit replies without new generation (taking it through the repair round reproduces the final draft exactly). Middle: paired differences, means over entries. Bottom: earlier scoring, pooled over facts}{table.24}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces Claims about the hidden papers in the second-hand draft (2,308 claims; 2,208 after collapsing a statement repeated in two paragraphs), audited against what the writer saw and against the full text. \emph  {own}: the auditor's quote is in the paper's title or abstract; \emph  {second-hand}: in a later paper's passage; \emph  {none}: no quote (judged unsupported or contradicted against what the writer saw). Middle and bottom: second-hand claims by passage kind and by the number of other references the passage cites (few = at most 2). Full texts exclude supplementary material, so ``unsupported'' is an upper bound on error; ``contradicted'' is not affected in the same way.}}{29}{table.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_secondhand_claims}{{25}{29}{Claims about the hidden papers in the second-hand draft (2,308 claims; 2,208 after collapsing a statement repeated in two paragraphs), audited against what the writer saw and against the full text. \emph {own}: the auditor's quote is in the paper's title or abstract; \emph {second-hand}: in a later paper's passage; \emph {none}: no quote (judged unsupported or contradicted against what the writer saw). Middle and bottom: second-hand claims by passage kind and by the number of other references the passage cites (few = at most 2). Full texts exclude supplementary material, so ``unsupported'' is an upper bound on error; ``contradicted'' is not affected in the same way}{table.25}{}}
